Template: sysible/tools
Type: multiselect
Choices: terraform, vault, consul, nomad, packer, boundary, aws-cli
Default:
Description: Optional software to install
 These tools are NOT bundled in the Sysible Server image, so they are
 offered here as a choice. HashiCorp's tools (terraform, vault, consul, nomad,
 packer, boundary) are BUSL-1.1 licensed, not open source; selecting them means
 you accept HashiCorp's licence (https://www.hashicorp.com/bsl). aws-cli is
 installed from Amazon's official channel.
 .
 Anything you select is installed automatically the first time this system boots
 with a working network connection. OpenTofu (the open Terraform drop-in),
 gcloud, the Azure CLI, Docker, kubectl, Helm and Ansible are already included.
 .
 You can add or remove these tools at any time later with:  sudo sysible-tools

Template: sysible/apps
Type: multiselect
Choices: slop (one gateway in front of all three), controller (fleet console), slep (infra automation), connect (browser terminal)
Default: slop (one gateway in front of all three)
Description: Sysible software to set up on first boot
 Tick what this server should run. These are the same four choices that
 `sudo install-sysible` offers after the install, so nothing chosen here is
 final.
 .
 "slop" puts the Controller, SLEP and Connect behind one front door at
 https://slop.lan/ with a single sign-in. It is the recommended choice and it
 already covers all three, so ticking it alongside the others adds nothing --
 if it is ticked, it is what gets installed.
 .
 The other three are the apps on their own addresses: controller is the fleet
 console, slep is infrastructure automation, connect is a terminal in the
 browser.
 .
 Tick nothing to set nothing up. Any of this can be changed afterwards with:
 sudo install-sysible
 .
 Whatever you pick is installed on the first boot with a working network: the
 source is cloned from GitHub and the containers are built from Docker Hub, so
 it needs both and it is not quick. Nothing listens on the network until it
 completes.
